    "content": "<!-- wp:cil/hero {\"sub\":\"Two experienced practitioners who have trained UK and International doctors. Local anaesthetic every time.\",\"html\":\"\",\"facts\":[],\"eyebrow\":\"CQC registered · Edgware, North-West London\",\"title\":\"Dedicated Circumcision Clinic in London\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book online\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/book/\",\"phoneLabel\":\"Call 020 8951 3794\",\"phoneUrl\":\"tel:+442089513794\",\"showFacts\":true} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/groups {\"items\":[{\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/babies/\",\"title\":\"Babies and toddlers\",\"age\":\"Best under one month old\",\"price\":\"From £200\",\"cta\":\"Baby circumcision, from £200\",\"blurb\":\"Circumcision is commonly carried out using the Plastibell or Circumplast ring method. For young babies, the procedure itself is usually less than 10 minutes and no stitches are required with the ring method. Bath him straight away.\"},{\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/children/\",\"title\":\"Children and teenagers\",\"age\":\"One to seventeen years\",\"price\":\"From £300\",\"cta\":\"Circumcision for boys, from £300\",\"blurb\":\"Older children are commonly treated using the forceps-guided traditional method with thermal cautery resulting in minimal bleeding. We explain the procedure in an age-appropriate way and provide parents with detailed aftercare instructions.\"},{\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\",\"title\":\"Adults\",\"age\":\"Eighteen and over\",\"price\":\"From £680\",\"cta\":\"Adult circumcision, from £680\",\"blurb\":\"We provide adult circumcision for religious, cultural, personal and medical reasons, including foreskin problems such as phimosis, paraphimosis, balanitis and BXO. We also assess patients seeking re-circumcision or revision procedures.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/trust-strip /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/home-clinic-introduction -->\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"clinic-introduction\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"clinic-introduction\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-home-intro\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-home-intro\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision in London at Beverley Clinic provides male circumcision for infants, babies, children, teenagers, boys and adult men. Our two circumcision practitioners have more than 40 years of combined experience in the UK and abroad and have carried out thousands of successful circumcisions across all age groups.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We understand that choosing circumcision for yourself or your child is an important decision. Our aim is to explain the procedure clearly, answer your questions and support you from the initial enquiry through to aftercare and healing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision may be requested for religious (such as Muslim and Jewish), cultural, personal or medical reasons. Every patient is assessed individually, and the method used depends on age, anatomy and clinical circumstances.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>CQC registered clinic in North-West London</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>More than 40 years of combined practitioner experience</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Circumcision for babies, children, teenagers and adults</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Local anaesthetic used for circumcisions, with the area checked before the procedure begins</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Plastibell / Circumplast ring method commonly used for babies and toddlers</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Forceps-guided (traditional) method with thermal cautery commonly used for older children and adults</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Written aftercare information and preparation videos</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Next-day follow-up call</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Free follow-up appointments during the healing period</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>GP letter available to update medical records</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>School or work letters available where appropriate</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>English, Arabic, Urdu, Hindi, Punjabi and Turkish spoken</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section --><!-- /wp:cil/home-clinic-introduction -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/home-additional-sections -->\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"why-patients-come-to-us\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"why-patients-come-to-us\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Why patients come to us\",\"lede\":\"\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Specialist focus\",\"body\":\"Circumcision is a core part of our day-to-day clinical work rather than an occasional procedure. Our practitioners have extensive experience in circumcision and have also trained doctors from the UK and abroad in circumcision techniques and patient care.\"},{\"title\":\"All ages\",\"body\":\"We provide circumcision for babies, toddlers, children, teenagers and adults, using techniques appropriate to the patient's age, anatomy and individual circumstances.\"},{\"title\":\"Continuity of care\",\"body\":\"Our care does not end when the procedure is finished. Patients and parents receive preparation information before treatment, detailed written aftercare afterwards, a next-day follow-up call and ongoing support throughout the healing period.\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted by patients and parents\",\"body\":\"Much of our work comes through word-of-mouth recommendations from previous patients and families. We are proud that patients continue to recommend Beverley Clinic to their friends, relatives and communities.\"},{\"title\":\"Thousands of patient reviews\",\"body\":\"We have received thousands of 5 star reviews from patients and parents who have used our service. Read about their experiences on Google, Trustpilot and Yell.com.\"},{\"title\":\"Convenient North-West London location\",\"body\":\"Our clinic is located in Edgware, North-West London, with good public transport links and free street parking nearby at all times.\"}],\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group \"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Circumcision for medical reasons\",\"display\":\"d-1\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision is not only performed for religious (Islam and Judaism), cultural or personal reasons. It can also be recommended to treat certain medical conditions affecting the foreskin or penis. We assess each patient individually and will discuss whether circumcision or an alternative treatment is most appropriate.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Phimosis (tight foreskin)\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003ePhimosis occurs when the foreskin is too tight to retract comfortably over the head of the penis (glans). It can cause discomfort, difficulty retracting the foreskin and problems with hygiene, and in some patients circumcision provides a long-term solution.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWhen circumcision is performed for phimosis, it is important that the tight or scarred area of foreskin is adequately treated. The technique is therefore tailored to the individual patient\\u0026#039;s anatomy and the extent of the tightness or scarring.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about phimosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Recurrent balanitis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBalanitis is inflammation of the head of the penis (glans), which can cause redness, soreness, irritation and discomfort. Recurrent episodes can sometimes be associated with a tight foreskin, particularly where the foreskin is difficult to retract and cleaning underneath it is challenging.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWhere balanitis keeps returning, we can assess the foreskin and discuss whether circumcision may be appropriate.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/balanitis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about balanitis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"BXO / lichen sclerosis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBXO (balanitis xerotica obliterans), also known as male genital lichen sclerosis, can affect the foreskin and cause whitening, thickening, scarring and progressive tightness.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIt can sometimes resemble phimosis, but the presence of scarring means careful assessment is important. Circumcision may be recommended where the foreskin is significantly affected.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/bxo/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about BXO / lichen sclerosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Paraphimosis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eParaphimosis occurs when the foreskin has been pulled back behind the head of the penis and cannot be returned to its normal position. This can cause increasing swelling and pain and, in some circumstances, requires urgent medical treatment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf you currently have a painful, swollen foreskin trapped behind the head of the penis, particularly if the swelling is increasing or you are having difficulty passing urine, seek urgent medical attention rather than waiting for a routine clinic appointment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/paraphimosis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about paraphimosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Tight frenulum\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe frenulum is the band of tissue on the underside of the penis connecting the foreskin to the head of the penis (glans). If it is unusually short, tight or scarred, it can cause pulling, pain, bleeding or downward curvature of the glans, particularly during an erection or sexual activity.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision is not always necessary for a tight frenulum. In suitable patients, releasing or lengthening the frenulum can treat the problem while preserving the foreskin.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/procedures/frenuloplasty/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about frenuloplasty and tight frenulum →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Buried penis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eA buried or hidden penis is where some or all of the penis is concealed within the surrounding pubic tissue. This can sometimes be associated with excess fatty tissue around the pubic area, although there are other causes.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eRecognising a buried penis before circumcision is important because it can influence both the procedure and the aftercare required. Our practitioners will assess this and explain any additional care that may be needed following circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/buried-penis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about buried penis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}],\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group \"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Circumcision methods used at our London clinic\",\"display\":\"d-1\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>There are several ways to perform a circumcision, and no single method is suitable for every patient. At Beverley Clinic, we select the circumcision technique according to the patient&#039;s age, anatomy, reason for circumcision and findings on examination.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our practitioners have extensive experience in circumcising babies, children, teenagers and adults and use different techniques according to the individual patient.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Plastibell and Circumplast circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor babies and younger children, we commonly use the Plastibell or Circumplast ring method where clinically suitable.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eA correctly sized plastic ring is positioned over the head of the penis (glans) and underneath the foreskin. The foreskin is secured around the ring, allowing the unwanted foreskin to separate naturally as the area heals.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOne advantage of this technique is that stitches are not required. The plastic ring remains in place after leaving the clinic and usually separates and falls off naturally during the healing process. If it does not fall off naturally, we book a ring removal follow up at no extra cost and this usually takes a few seconds to remove.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eParents receive detailed aftercare instructions explaining how to care for their baby or child while the ring is in place, what to expect during normal healing and when to contact us for advice. We also provide follow-up support throughout the healing period.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/babies/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about baby circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Forceps-guided circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor older children, teenagers and adults, we commonly use a forceps-guided circumcision technique with thermal cautery.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThe foreskin is carefully positioned to determine the appropriate amount to remove. A specialist surgical forceps is used to guide the circumcision and protect the underlying structures, while thermal cautery helps control bleeding during the procedure.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eDepending on the patient\\u0026#039;s age, anatomy and the wound following circumcision, the skin may be closed using dissolvable stitches, medical skin glue, a combination of both, or occasionally neither.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003ePatients receive detailed aftercare instructions explaining how to care for the wound, what to expect during healing and when they can gradually return to normal activities.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/children/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about child circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Why don't we use the same circumcision method for everyone?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision should be tailored to the individual rather than using the same technique for every patient.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eA method suitable for a young baby may not be appropriate for an older child or adult. Before deciding which technique to use, we consider the patient\\u0026#039;s age, penile anatomy, foreskin development, reason for circumcision and any medical condition affecting the foreskin or penis.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThis is particularly important when treating conditions such as phimosis or BXO (lichen sclerosis), where scarring or a tight band of foreskin may affect how the circumcision needs to be performed. Additional consideration may also be required for patients with a buried penis or those seeking re-circumcision or revision surgery.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eEvery patient is assessed before the procedure so that we can select the method most appropriate for their individual circumstances and explain what to expect from the procedure, aftercare and recovery.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about adult circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}],\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section --><!-- /wp:cil/home-additional-sections -->\n\n\n<!-- wp:cil/process {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Next steps\",\"lede\":\"\",\"items\":[{\"h\":\"Contact us\",\"p\":\"Ask questions by telephone, WhatsApp or the website enquiry form.\"},{\"h\":\"Preparation\",\"p\":\"We send you written and video information to prepare you on what to bring, what to expect on the day and the expected aftercare following the circumcision.\"},{\"h\":\"Procedure\",\"p\":\"Local anaesthetic is given and the area is checked before the procedure begins.\"},{\"h\":\"Aftercare\",\"p\":\"You leave with written instructions. We contact you the following day to answer any further questions you may have and offer follow-up appointments during healing if needed.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/home-callback {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"When we may postpone\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eWho is suitable for circumcision?\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe circumcise males of all ages and backgrounds, so whether it is for religious, cultural or medical reasons, we have you covered. Let us know when booking what your main reason for circumcising and we will accommodate you accordingly.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOur 2 practitioners are Muslim and we treat a big portion of the Muslim community in London and from other parts of the UK. We also get patients from the Jewish community coming in for religious circumcisions.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eSome patients get circumcised to meet cultural requirements such as Filipinos, certain parts of Africa, Fiji and other countries where circumcision is an important part of their culture.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe also get a big portion of patients who have a medical reason for getting circumcised, most common is a tight foreskin (phimosis and paraphimosis), inflammation of the head of the penis (balanitis) as well as short and scarred frenulum.\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"urgentTitle\":\"Urgent symptoms\",\"urgentBody\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eSeek urgent medical assessment if a pulled-back foreskin is trapped behind the head of the penis and swelling, if the patient cannot pass urine, or if there is spreading redness with fever. These symptoms should not wait for a routine clinic appointment and you should contact 999.\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"cardHtml\":\"\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eWant to ask before you book?\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe often call you back within a few minutes, but always within the same day even during busy times. Monday – Saturday 09:00–17:00.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eName, phone number\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003ePatient DOB\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eAnything you would like us to know (optional)\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"cardTitle\":\"Ask before you book\",\"cardEyebrow\":\"Request a call back\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/intro {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Location\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBeverley Clinic, 78 Beverley Drive, Edgware, HA8 5NE. The clinic is in North-West London with nearby public transport links and plenty of free street parking. Queensbury Underground station (8 mins walk) on the Jubilee line and Burnt Oak station on the Northern line (20 mins walk) are both nearby.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/reviews {\"body\":\"Most of our patients arrive because somebody they trust sent them. The families who come back are the part we are proudest of: some return after many years whenever there is a new son, others bring a brother, then a nephew, then a cousin. We have families we have now seen across three children and the better part of a decade.\",\"quotes\":[{\"name\":\"Mustafa Butt\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision, three weeks old\",\"quote\":\"The receptionist explained the procedure clearly and put us at ease straight away. The doctor was thorough and professional, explained everything beforehand, and stayed calm and reassuring throughout. He took the time to go through the aftercare in detail.\"},{\"name\":\"Wajahat Murtaza\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision\",\"quote\":\"Smooth and efficient from start to finish. Dr Haidar is professional and experienced, we were given all the information we needed, and a follow-up call was made as well, which is a nice thing to do. The ring came off after a week and my son is doing well.\"},{\"name\":\"Sara Salmanpour\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision, two months old\",\"quote\":\"As first-time parents we were naturally anxious, but the team made us feel completely at ease. The doctor explained the procedure in detail and answered every concern with patience. They gave us the option to contact them any time afterwards, which was a huge relief.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"anchor\":\"our-clinics\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"our-clinics\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Our clinics\",\"heading\":\"London, Luton, Southampton and Birmingham\",\"lede\":\"The London clinic in Edgware can be booked online. Luton, Southampton and Birmingham are booked by telephone.\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"London\",\"title\":\"London — Edgware\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003e78 Beverley Drive, Edgware HA8 5NE\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book a consultation\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/book/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn\",\"cta2Label\":\"View London clinic\",\"cta2Url\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/contact/\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Luton\",\"title\":\"Luton\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003eLiverpool Road Health Centre\\u003cbr\\u003eLuton LU1 1HH\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Luton clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/luton-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Southampton\",\"title\":\"Southampton\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003eEastleigh Health Centre\\u003cbr\\u003eEastleigh SO50 9AG\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Southampton clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/southampton-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Birmingham\",\"title\":\"Birmingham\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003eSoho Health Centre\\u003cbr\\u003eLouise Road\\u003cbr\\u003eBirmingham B21 9RY\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Birmingham clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/birmingham-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"}],\"columns\":\"g-4\",\"headingLevel\":2} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/cta-band /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/faq {\"heading\":\"The questions we are asked most\",\"items\":[{\"q\":\"Is the circumcision painful?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eNo. Every patient has local anaesthetic, at every age. It is safe, and it is illegal to circumcise without it.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe do not simply assume it has worked. Once it has had time, we test the area and show you that no pain is felt, and we only begin once you tell us you are happy to proceed. Babies sometimes cry anyway: the anaesthetic removes pain but keeps ordinary touch sensation, which is painless, and an unfamiliar touch there is enough to make a baby object.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"How long does it take?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor a baby, the circumcision itself is about ten minutes, and the anaesthetic lasts around two hours afterwards. Older children and adults take longer. Allow about an hour for the visit either way, which covers the consultation, consent, the anaesthetic working and going through aftercare before you leave.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Which method do you use?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor babies and toddlers, we often use the ring method (e.g. Plastibell or Circumplast). The advantages are that it does not require any stitches, you can bath your son normally and often comes off by itself within 3-14 days similar to the umbilical cord. The disadvantages is that it sometimes does not come off automatically and will require us to remove it but this often takes less than 5 seconds.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOlder children and adults are often circumcised with the forceps guided (traditional) method using thermal cautery which seals as it cuts, resulting in minimal bleeding if any. We close the wound using skin glue, stitches or a combination of both depending on the individual patient. Both of these come off naturally.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"What is the best age?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eUnder one month old, if the choice is open to you. At that age it is quick and simple and healing is faster. We circumcise routinely at every age after that, right through to adults, so it is never too late.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you carry out religious circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes, and it is a large part of what we do. Our Muslim practitioners carry out the procedure according to the Sunnah, and we routinely cater for all faiths and backgrounds. \\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/religious/\\u0022\\u003eMore about religious and cultural circumcision\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can you correct a circumcision done elsewhere?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Parents bring sons to us from across the UK and from abroad to tidy up work done somewhere else, and adults come for the same reason. It ranges from scar revision to tightening a loose result. \\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/re-circumcision/\\u0022\\u003eMore about re-circumcision\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do I need to do anything to prepare?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eVery little, because it is done under local anaesthetic. There is no fasting. When you book we send you videos on how to prepare and what to expect from start to finish, and the page for your age group lists exactly what to bring.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Could the NHS do this instead?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWhere there is a medical need, yes, and if you can wait that is a reasonable choice. From what our patients tell us, the wait runs beyond a year. Religious and cultural circumcision is not funded. Give us a call if you would like to discuss further.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
}
